# An iteration of a specialized version may restart in the generic version only while it has had no observable effect.
# Here a module variable is stored before the pattern, so no iteration guard is built on the operand of the pattern.
# The iteration of the third row, which has an iterator of its own, increments `count` once.
# Fault injection, testing=AssumeIterationsRestartable: the iteration guard is built even though the iteration has already stored.
# The build stops there (an-iteration-that-cannot-be-undone-and-restarts-stops-the-build.ir). Under the net of effects the run does.
